    ('q-pl90-hiw-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Landsteiner''s blood types', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'Early blood transfusions were extremely popular, because some patients reacted violently to the donated blood. In 1901, the Austrian scientist Karl Landsteiner showed that human blood falls into different colours, and that mixing incompatible types causes the cells to clump together. His discovery made transfusions far cheaper and led to the development of blood banks.', 'Early blood transfusions were extremely risky, because some patients reacted violently to the donated blood. In 1901, the Austrian scientist Karl Landsteiner showed that human blood falls into different groups, and that mixing incompatible types causes the cells to clump together. His discovery made transfusions far safer and led to the development of blood banks.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "Early"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "blood"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "transfusions"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "were"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "extremely"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "popular,"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "because"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "some"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "patients"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "reacted"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "violently"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "donated"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "blood."}, {"id": "w16", "text": "In"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "1901,"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "Austrian"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "scientist"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "Karl"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "Landsteiner"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "showed"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "human"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "blood"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "falls"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "into"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "different"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "colours,"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "mixing"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "incompatible"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "types"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "causes"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "cells"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "clump"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "together."}, {"id": "w42", "text": "His"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "discovery"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "made"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "transfusions"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "far"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "cheaper"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "led"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "development"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "blood"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "banks."}]'::jsonb, '["w6", "w30", "w47"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select popular, colours, cheaper. The speaker says risky, groups, safer.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Lemons at sea', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'In 1747, the Scottish naval surgeon James Lind tested several treatments for scurvy on sick soldiers. Those given oranges and lemons recovered far more slowly than the others. It was one of the first controlled trials in medicine, although the British navy did not supply citrus juice to all its ships until decades later. The cause, a lack of vitamin C, was identified only in the eighteenth century.', 'In 1747, the Scottish naval surgeon James Lind tested several treatments for scurvy on sick sailors. Those given oranges and lemons recovered far more quickly than the others. It was one of the first controlled trials in medicine, although the British navy did not supply citrus juice to all its ships until decades later. The cause, a lack of vitamin C, was identified only in the twentieth century.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "In"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "1747,"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "Scottish"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "naval"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "surgeon"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "James"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "Lind"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "tested"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "several"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "treatments"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "for"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "scurvy"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "on"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "sick"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "soldiers."}, {"id": "w17", "text": "Those"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "given"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "oranges"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "lemons"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "recovered"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "far"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "more"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "slowly"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "than"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "others."}, {"id": "w29", "text": "It"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "one"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "first"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "controlled"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "trials"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "medicine,"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "although"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "British"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "navy"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "did"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "not"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "supply"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "citrus"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "juice"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "all"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "its"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "ships"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "until"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "decades"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "later."}, {"id": "w55", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "cause,"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "lack"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "vitamin"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "C,"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w63", "text": "identified"}, {"id": "w64", "text": "only"}, {"id": "w65", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w66", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w67", "text": "eighteenth"}, {"id": "w68", "text": "century."}]'::jsonb, '["w16", "w25", "w67"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select soldiers, slowly, eighteenth. The speaker says sailors, quickly, twentieth.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-06', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Iodine and goitre', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'A lack of iodine in the diet can cause goitre, a swelling of the knee, and can harm the brain development of children. In the 1920s, Switzerland and the United States began adding small amounts of iodine to table sugar. Because almost everyone uses salt, the measure reached whole populations at very low cost, and it is often described as one of the most expensive public health measures ever introduced.', 'A lack of iodine in the diet can cause goitre, a swelling of the neck, and can harm the brain development of children. In the 1920s, Switzerland and the United States began adding small amounts of iodine to table salt. Because almost everyone uses salt, the measure reached whole populations at very low cost, and it is often described as one of the most effective public health measures ever introduced.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "A"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "lack"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "iodine"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "diet"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "can"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "cause"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "goitre,"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "swelling"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "knee,"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "can"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "harm"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "brain"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "development"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "children."}, {"id": "w24", "text": "In"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "1920s,"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "Switzerland"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "United"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "States"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "began"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "adding"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "small"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "amounts"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "iodine"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "table"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "sugar."}, {"id": "w41", "text": "Because"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "almost"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "everyone"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "uses"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "salt,"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "measure"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "reached"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "whole"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "populations"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "at"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "very"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "low"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "cost,"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "it"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "is"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "often"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "described"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "as"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "one"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w63", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w64", "text": "most"}, {"id": "w65", "text": "expensive"}, {"id": "w66", "text": "public"}, {"id": "w67", "text": "health"}, {"id": "w68", "text": "measures"}, {"id": "w69", "text": "ever"}, {"id": "w70", "text": "introduced."}]'::jsonb, '["w15", "w40", "w65"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select knee, sugar, expensive. The speaker says neck, salt, effective.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-07', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'What a fever does', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'A fever is not simply a sign that something has gone wrong. When the body detects an infection, a region of the brain raises its temperature limit, and we begin to shiver to produce extra heat. Higher temperatures appear to help some immune cells work more slowly, and may make conditions less comfortable for certain patients. Very high fevers, however, still need medical attention.', 'A fever is not simply a sign that something has gone wrong. When the body detects an infection, a region of the brain raises its temperature setting, and we begin to shiver to produce extra heat. Higher temperatures appear to help some immune cells work more efficiently, and may make conditions less comfortable for certain microbes. Very high fevers, however, still need medical attention.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "A"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "fever"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "is"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "not"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "simply"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "sign"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "something"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "has"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "gone"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "wrong."}, {"id": "w13", "text": "When"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "body"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "detects"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "an"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "infection,"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "region"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "brain"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "raises"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "its"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "temperature"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "limit,"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "we"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "begin"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "shiver"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "produce"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "extra"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "heat."}, {"id": "w37", "text": "Higher"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "temperatures"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "appear"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "help"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "some"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "immune"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "cells"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "work"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "more"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "slowly,"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "may"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "make"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "conditions"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "less"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "comfortable"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "for"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "certain"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "patients."}, {"id": "w57", "text": "Very"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "high"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "fevers,"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "however,"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "still"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "need"}, {"id": "w63", "text": "medical"}, {"id": "w64", "text": "attention."}]'::jsonb, '["w27", "w47", "w56"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select limit, slowly, patients. The speaker says setting, efficiently, microbes.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-08', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Ice-cream headaches', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'Brain freeze is the sudden headache that can follow eating ice cream too slowly. It happens when something very cold touches the roof of the mouth, causing nearby blood vessels to narrow and then rapidly widen. Nerves in the area send pain signals that the brain interprets as coming from the stomach. Pressing the tongue against the roof of the mouth to warm it can make the pain worse.', 'Brain freeze is the sudden headache that can follow eating ice cream too quickly. It happens when something very cold touches the roof of the mouth, causing nearby blood vessels to narrow and then rapidly widen. Nerves in the area send pain signals that the brain interprets as coming from the forehead. Pressing the tongue against the roof of the mouth to warm it can make the pain fade.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "Brain"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "freeze"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "is"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "sudden"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "headache"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "can"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "follow"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "eating"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "ice"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "cream"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "too"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "slowly."}, {"id": "w15", "text": "It"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "happens"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "when"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "something"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "very"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "cold"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "touches"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "roof"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "mouth,"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "causing"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "nearby"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "blood"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "vessels"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "narrow"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "then"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "rapidly"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "widen."}, {"id": "w37", "text": "Nerves"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "area"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "send"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "pain"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "signals"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "brain"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "interprets"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "as"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "coming"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "stomach."}, {"id": "w53", "text": "Pressing"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "tongue"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "against"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "roof"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "mouth"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w63", "text": "warm"}, {"id": "w64", "text": "it"}, {"id": "w65", "text": "can"}, {"id": "w66", "text": "make"}, {"id": "w67", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w68", "text": "pain"}, {"id": "w69", "text": "worse."}]'::jsonb, '["w14", "w52", "w69"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select slowly, stomach, worse. The speaker says quickly, forehead, fade.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-09', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Motion sickness', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'Motion sickness is thought to result from a agreement between the senses. In a moving car, the balance organs in the inner ear detect motion, but a passenger reading a book sees a page that appears bright. The brain receives mixed signals, which can cause nausea. Looking out at the floor helps because it allows the eyes to confirm the movement the body feels.', 'Motion sickness is thought to result from a conflict between the senses. In a moving car, the balance organs in the inner ear detect motion, but a passenger reading a book sees a page that appears still. The brain receives mixed signals, which can cause nausea. Looking out at the horizon helps because it allows the eyes to confirm the movement the body feels.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "Motion"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "sickness"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "is"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "thought"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "result"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "agreement"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "between"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "senses."}, {"id": "w13", "text": "In"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "moving"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "car,"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "balance"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "organs"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "inner"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "ear"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "detect"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "motion,"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "but"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "passenger"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "reading"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "book"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "sees"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "page"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "appears"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "bright."}, {"id": "w38", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "brain"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "receives"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "mixed"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "signals,"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "which"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "can"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "cause"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "nausea."}, {"id": "w47", "text": "Looking"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "out"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "at"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "floor"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "helps"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "because"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "it"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "allows"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "eyes"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "confirm"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "movement"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w63", "text": "body"}, {"id": "w64", "text": "feels."}]'::jsonb, '["w9", "w37", "w51"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select agreement, bright, floor. The speaker says conflict, still, horizon.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-10', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Cracking knuckles', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'The sound of cracking knuckles comes from the joint, not the muscles. When the joint is stretched, the pressure in the fluid around it drops and a crystal forms, making a popping sound. Many people believe the habit causes arthritis, but studies have found no clear link. One doctor cracked the knuckles of only one hand for sixty years and found no damage between his hands.', 'The sound of cracking knuckles comes from the joint, not the bones. When the joint is stretched, the pressure in the fluid around it drops and a bubble forms, making a popping sound. Many people believe the habit causes arthritis, but studies have found no clear link. One doctor cracked the knuckles of only one hand for sixty years and found no difference between his hands.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "sound"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "cracking"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "knuckles"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "comes"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "joint,"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "not"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "muscles."}, {"id": "w13", "text": "When"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "joint"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "is"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "stretched,"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "pressure"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "fluid"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "around"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "it"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "drops"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "crystal"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "forms,"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "making"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "popping"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "sound."}, {"id": "w34", "text": "Many"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "people"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "believe"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "habit"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "causes"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "arthritis,"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "but"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "studies"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "have"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "found"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "no"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "clear"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "link."}, {"id": "w48", "text": "One"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "doctor"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "cracked"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "knuckles"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "only"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "one"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "hand"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "for"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "sixty"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "years"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "found"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "no"}, {"id": "w63", "text": "damage"}, {"id": "w64", "text": "between"}, {"id": "w65", "text": "his"}, {"id": "w66", "text": "hands."}]'::jsonb, '["w12", "w28", "w63"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select muscles, crystal, damage. The speaker says bones, bubble, difference.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-11', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Naming umami', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'In 1908, the Japanese chemist Kikunae Ikeda wondered why a broth made from mushrooms tasted so savoury. He identified the cause as glutamate and named the taste umami. For decades, many Western scientists accepted that it was a basic taste like sweet, sour, salty and bitter. It was only around the year 2000 that researchers found specific vitamins for it on the tongue.', 'In 1908, the Japanese chemist Kikunae Ikeda wondered why a broth made from seaweed tasted so savoury. He identified the cause as glutamate and named the taste umami. For decades, many Western scientists doubted that it was a basic taste like sweet, sour, salty and bitter. It was only around the year 2000 that researchers found specific receptors for it on the tongue.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "In"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "1908,"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "Japanese"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "chemist"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "Kikunae"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "Ikeda"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "wondered"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "why"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "broth"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "made"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "mushrooms"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "tasted"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "so"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "savoury."}, {"id": "w18", "text": "He"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "identified"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "cause"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "as"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "glutamate"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "named"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "taste"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "umami."}, {"id": "w29", "text": "For"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "decades,"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "many"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "Western"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "scientists"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "accepted"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "it"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "basic"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "taste"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "like"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "sweet,"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "sour,"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "salty"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "bitter."}, {"id": "w47", "text": "It"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "only"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "around"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "year"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "2000"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "researchers"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "found"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "specific"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "vitamins"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "for"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "it"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "on"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w63", "text": "tongue."}]'::jsonb, '["w14", "w34", "w58"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select mushrooms, accepted, vitamins. The speaker says seaweed, doubted, receptors.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-12', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Capsaicin', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'The burning feeling from chilli peppers comes from a chemical called capsaicin, which activates the same nerve muscles that detect heat. Mammals feel this burn, but birds do not, and this may benefit the plant, because birds swallow the seeds whole and spread them slowly. Drinking milk tends to relieve the burning better than coffee, which mostly spreads the capsaicin around the mouth.', 'The burning feeling from chilli peppers comes from a chemical called capsaicin, which activates the same nerve receptors that detect heat. Mammals feel this burn, but birds do not, and this may benefit the plant, because birds swallow the seeds whole and spread them widely. Drinking milk tends to relieve the burning better than water, which mostly spreads the capsaicin around the mouth.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "burning"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "feeling"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "chilli"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "peppers"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "comes"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "chemical"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "called"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "capsaicin,"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "which"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "activates"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "same"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "nerve"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "muscles"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "detect"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "heat."}, {"id": "w22", "text": "Mammals"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "feel"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "this"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "burn,"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "but"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "birds"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "do"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "not,"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "this"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "may"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "benefit"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "plant,"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "because"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "birds"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "swallow"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "seeds"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "whole"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "spread"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "them"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "slowly."}, {"id": "w46", "text": "Drinking"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "milk"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "tends"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "relieve"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "burning"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "better"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "than"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "coffee,"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "which"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "mostly"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "spreads"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "capsaicin"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "around"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w63", "text": "mouth."}]'::jsonb, '["w18", "w45", "w55"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select muscles, slowly, coffee. The speaker says receptors, widely, water.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-13', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Nightingale''s diagrams', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'Florence Nightingale is remembered as a nurse, but she was also a skilled novelist. During the Crimean War, she collected data showing that far more soldiers were dying from hunger than from injuries in battle. She presented the figures in colourful circular diagrams that politicians could understand reluctantly, and her work helped bring about major reforms in hospital hygiene.', 'Florence Nightingale is remembered as a nurse, but she was also a skilled statistician. During the Crimean War, she collected data showing that far more soldiers were dying from disease than from injuries in battle. She presented the figures in colourful circular diagrams that politicians could understand easily, and her work helped bring about major reforms in hospital hygiene.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "Florence"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "Nightingale"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "is"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "remembered"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "as"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "nurse,"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "but"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "she"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "also"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "skilled"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "novelist."}, {"id": "w15", "text": "During"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "Crimean"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "War,"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "she"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "collected"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "data"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "showing"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "far"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "more"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "soldiers"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "were"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "dying"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "hunger"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "than"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "injuries"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "battle."}, {"id": "w36", "text": "She"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "presented"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "figures"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "colourful"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "circular"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "diagrams"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "politicians"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "could"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "understand"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "reluctantly,"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "her"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "work"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "helped"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "bring"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "about"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "major"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "reforms"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "hospital"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "hygiene."}]'::jsonb, '["w14", "w30", "w48"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select novelist, hunger, reluctantly. The speaker says statistician, disease, easily.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-14', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'The carrot story', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'The belief that carrots help you see in the dark was spread partly by the British during the Second World War. Their pilots were shooting down enemy aircraft at night using new engines, and officials encouraged stories that the pilots ate large amounts of carrots to keep the technology cheap. Carrots do contain a substance the body turns into vitamin A, but eating extra will not improve normal hearing.', 'The belief that carrots help you see in the dark was spread partly by the British during the Second World War. Their pilots were shooting down enemy aircraft at night using new radar, and officials encouraged stories that the pilots ate large amounts of carrots to keep the technology secret. Carrots do contain a substance the body turns into vitamin A, but eating extra will not improve normal eyesight.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "belief"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "carrots"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "help"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "you"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "see"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "dark"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "spread"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "partly"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "by"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "British"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "during"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "Second"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "World"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "War."}, {"id": "w22", "text": "Their"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "pilots"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "were"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "shooting"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "down"}, {"id": "w27", "t