    ('q-pl90-hiw-15', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Oral rehydration', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'Diarrhoeal diseases such as cholera kill mainly by causing severe fever. In the 1960s and 1970s, researchers working in South Asia showed that a simple drink of clean water, salt and milk could replace lost fluids, because sugar helps the intestine absorb salt and water. This cheap treatment, known as oral rehydration solution, is credited with saving hundreds of lives.', 'Diarrhoeal diseases such as cholera kill mainly by causing severe dehydration. In the 1960s and 1970s, researchers working in South Asia showed that a simple drink of clean water, salt and sugar could replace lost fluids, because sugar helps the intestine absorb salt and water. This cheap treatment, known as oral rehydration solution, is credited with saving millions of lives.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "Diarrhoeal"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "diseases"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "such"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "as"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "cholera"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "kill"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "mainly"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "by"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "causing"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "severe"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "fever."}, {"id": "w12", "text": "In"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "1960s"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "1970s,"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "researchers"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "working"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "South"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "Asia"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "showed"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "simple"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "drink"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "clean"},