    ('q-pl90-hiw-27', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'The first underground railway', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'London''s Metropolitan Railway, opened in 1936, was the world''s first underground railway. Its trains were pulled by steam locomotives, so the tunnels were often filled with water, despite openings built to let it escape. Even so, the line was an immediate success, carrying tens of thousands of passengers on its first night.', 'London''s Metropolitan Railway, opened in 1863, was the world''s first underground railway. Its trains were pulled by steam locomotives, so the tunnels were often filled with smoke, despite openings built to let it escape. Even so, the line was an immediate success, carrying tens of thousands of passengers on its first day.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "London''s"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "Metropolitan"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "Railway,"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "opened"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "1936,"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "world''s"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "first"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "underground"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "railway."}, {"id": "w13", "text": "Its"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "trains"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "were"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "pulled"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "by"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "steam"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "locomotives,"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "so"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "tunnels"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "were"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "often"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "filled"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "with"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "water,"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "despite"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "openings"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "built"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "let"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "it"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "escape."}, {"id": "w35", "text": "Even"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "so,"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "line"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "an"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "immediate"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "success,"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "carrying"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "tens"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "thousands"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "passengers"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "on"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "its"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "first"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "night."}]'::jsonb, '["w6", "w27", "w52"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select 1936, water, night. The speaker says 1863, smoke, day.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-28', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Vulcanisation', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'In the early nineteenth century, natural rubber was of limited use because it became sticky in winter and brittle in cold weather. The American inventor Charles Goodyear spent years experimenting, and in 1839 he found that heating rubber with sugar made it strong and flexible at all temperatures. The process, called vulcanisation, made modern tyres possible, yet Goodyear died heavily in luxury.', 'In the early nineteenth century, natural rubber was of limited use because it became sticky in summer and brittle in cold weather. The American inventor Charles Goodyear spent years experimenting, and in 1839 he found that heating rubber with sulphur made it strong and flexible at all temperatures. The process, called vulcanisation, made modern tyres possible, yet Goodyear died heavily in debt.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "In"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "early"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "nineteenth"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "century,"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "natural"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "rubber"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "limited"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "use"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "because"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "it"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "became"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "sticky"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "winter"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "brittle"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "cold"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "weather."}, {"id": "w23", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "American"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "inventor"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "Charles"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "Goodyear"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "spent"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "years"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "experimenting,"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w32", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "1839"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "he"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "found"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "that"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "heating"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "rubber"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "with"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "sugar"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "made"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "it"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "strong"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "flexible"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "at"}, {"id": "w47", "text": "all"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "temperatures."}, {"id": "w49", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "process,"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "called"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "vulcanisation,"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "made"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "modern"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "tyres"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "possible,"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "yet"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "Goodyear"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "died"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "heavily"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "luxury."}]'::jsonb, '["w17", "w40", "w62"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select winter, sugar, luxury. The speaker says summer, sulphur, debt.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-29', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'The first lawn mower', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'The first lawn mower was invented in 1830 by the English engineer Edwin Budding, who got the idea from a machine used to trim the surface of paper in textile mills. Before this, lawns were cut by workers with scissors, which only the wealthy could afford. Budding''s mower made neat lawns possible for many more people and helped popularise sports played on ice, such as tennis.', 'The first lawn mower was invented in 1830 by the English engineer Edwin Budding, who got the idea from a machine used to trim the surface of cloth in textile mills. Before this, lawns were cut by workers with scythes, which only the wealthy could afford. Budding''s mower made neat lawns possible for many more people and helped popularise sports played on grass, such as tennis.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "first"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "lawn"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "mower"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "was"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "invented"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "1830"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "by"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "English"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "engineer"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "Edwin"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "Budding,"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "who"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "got"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "idea"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "a"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "machine"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "used"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "trim"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "surface"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "of"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "paper"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "textile"}, {"id": "w31", "text": "mills."}, {"id": "w32", "text": "Before"}, {"id": "w33", "text": "this,"}, {"id": "w34", "text": "lawns"}, {"id": "w35", "text": "were"}, {"id": "w36", "text": "cut"}, {"id": "w37", "text": "by"}, {"id": "w38", "text": "workers"}, {"id": "w39", "text": "with"}, {"id": "w40", "text": "scissors,"}, {"id": "w41", "text": "which"}, {"id": "w42", "text": "only"}, {"id": "w43", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w44", "text": "wealthy"}, {"id": "w45", "text": "could"}, {"id": "w46", "text": "afford."}, {"id": "w47", "text": "Budding''s"}, {"id": "w48", "text": "mower"}, {"id": "w49", "text": "made"}, {"id": "w50", "text": "neat"}, {"id": "w51", "text": "lawns"}, {"id": "w52", "text": "possible"}, {"id": "w53", "text": "for"}, {"id": "w54", "text": "many"}, {"id": "w55", "text": "more"}, {"id": "w56", "text": "people"}, {"id": "w57", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w58", "text": "helped"}, {"id": "w59", "text": "popularise"}, {"id": "w60", "text": "sports"}, {"id": "w61", "text": "played"}, {"id": "w62", "text": "on"}, {"id": "w63", "text": "ice,"}, {"id": "w64", "text": "such"}, {"id": "w65", "text": "as"}, {"id": "w66", "text": "tennis."}]'::jsonb, '["w28", "w40", "w63"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'Select paper, scissors, ice. The speaker says cloth, scythes, grass.', 'medium', 3, ARRAY['PTE', 'Original practice', 'Highlight Incorrect Word']::text[], true),
    ('q-pl90-hiw-30', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'The South Sea Bubble', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'In 1720, shares in Britain''s South Sea Company rose to extraordinary lows before collapsing within months. The company had promised enormous profits from trade with South America, but these profits never appeared. Many investors were rewarded, including, according to popular accounts, the scientist Isaac Newton, who is said to have remarked that he could calculate the motions of the heavenly bodies, but not the wisdom of people.', 'In 1720, shares in Britain''s South Sea Company rose to extraordinary levels before collapsing within months. The company had promised enormous profits from trade with South America, but these profits never appeared. Many investors were ruined, including, according to popular accounts, the scientist Isaac Newton, who is said to have remarked that he could calculate the motions of the heavenly bodies, but not the madness of people.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "In"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "1720,"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "shares"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "Britain''s"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "South"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "Sea"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "Company"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "rose"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "to"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "extraordinary"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "lows"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "before"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "collapsing"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "within"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "months."}, {"id": "w17", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "company"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "had"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "promised"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "enormous"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "profits"}, {"id": "w23", "text": "from"}, {"id": "w24", "text":