    ('q-pl90-hiw-31', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE']::text[], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-incorrect-word', 'Highlight Incorrect Word', 'Coubertin''s Games', 'You will hear a recording. Below is a transcription of the recording. Some words in the transcription differ from what the speaker said. Please click on the words that are different.', 'The modern Olympic Games were revived by the French educator Pierre de Coubertin, who believed sport could improve agriculture and international understanding. The first Games took place in Athens in 1896, with athletes from about fourteen cities. Only men competed; women took part for the first time four years later in Rome.', 'The modern Olympic Games were revived by the French educator Pierre de Coubertin, who believed sport could improve education and international understanding. The first Games took place in Athens in 1896, with athletes from about fourteen nations. Only men competed; women took part for the first time four years later in Paris.', 10, 120, '[{"id": "w1", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w2", "text": "modern"}, {"id": "w3", "text": "Olympic"}, {"id": "w4", "text": "Games"}, {"id": "w5", "text": "were"}, {"id": "w6", "text": "revived"}, {"id": "w7", "text": "by"}, {"id": "w8", "text": "the"}, {"id": "w9", "text": "French"}, {"id": "w10", "text": "educator"}, {"id": "w11", "text": "Pierre"}, {"id": "w12", "text": "de"}, {"id": "w13", "text": "Coubertin,"}, {"id": "w14", "text": "who"}, {"id": "w15", "text": "believed"}, {"id": "w16", "text": "sport"}, {"id": "w17", "text": "could"}, {"id": "w18", "text": "improve"}, {"id": "w19", "text": "agriculture"}, {"id": "w20", "text": "and"}, {"id": "w21", "text": "international"}, {"id": "w22", "text": "understanding."}, {"id": "w23", "text": "The"}, {"id": "w24", "text": "first"}, {"id": "w25", "text": "Games"}, {"id": "w26", "text": "took"}, {"id": "w27", "text": "place"}, {"id": "w28", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w29", "text": "Athens"}, {"id": "w30", "text": "in"}, {"id": "w